'''R2-Q2''' was an [[R2-series astromech droid]] manufactured by [[Industrial Automaton]] that was attached to the [[501st Legion]] of the [[Galactic Empire]]. During the [[Galactic Civil War]], it was part of the team that [[Secret mission to Tatooine|boarded]] the ''[[Tantive IV]]'' to root out [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel]] [[Spy|spies]]. [[Standard decade|Decades]] later, R2-Q2 was a member of the [[Resistance]].

==Biography==
R2-Q2 was an [[R2-series astromech droid]]<ref name="WCF" /> that was manufactured by [[Industrial Automaton]].<ref name="R2-Q2" /> During the [[Galactic Civil War]] between the [[Galactic Empire]] and the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]],<ref name="A New Hope" /> the [[astromech droid]] served the Empire.<ref name="R2-Q2" /> In [[1 BBY]],<ref name="ANHDate">{{FilmDate|IV|1}}</ref> it was stationed on board the [[Imperial I-class Star Destroyer|''Imperial I''-class Star Destroyer]]<ref name="A New Hope" /> ''[[Devastator]]''<ref name="Raymus">{{StoryCite|story=Raymus|book=From a Certain Point of View}}</ref> when the [[starship]] chased the rebel [[CR90 corvette]]<ref name="A New Hope" /> ''[[Tantive IV]]'' from the [[Scarif system]] to the [[Tatoo system]] following the [[Battle of Scarif]].<ref name="Raymus" />

[[File:R2Q2-ANH.png|thumb|250px|left|R2-Q2 was part of the team that boarded the ''Tantive IV''.]]
After the [[Star Destroyer]] disabled the [[corvette]],<ref name="Raymus" /> R2-Q2 was part of the team that boarded the rebel ship,<ref name="R2-Q2" /> which they suspected was carrying the [[Death Star plans|plans]] for the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] [[superweapon]],<ref name="A New Hope" /> which had been stolen at [[Scarif]].<ref name="Raymus" /> R2-Q2 was tasked with seeking out evidence of the ship's ties to the Rebellion<ref name="R2-Q2" /> and rolled down one of the corvette's corridors alongside fellow Imperial astromech [[R4-M9]] and several Imperial [[stormtrooper]]s escorting a group of captive rebel combatants. The crew of the ''Tantive IV'' were ultimately arrested as rebels, but the Empire failed to retrieve the [[Death Star]] plans.<ref name="A New Hope" />

[[File:Resistance group shot R2-KT.jpg|thumb|250px|right|By the destruction of Starkiller Base, R2-Q2 was serving the Resistance on D'Qar.]]
By [[34 ABY]],<ref name="TFADate">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the events of {{Film|VII}} to [[34 ABY]].</ref> R2-Q2 no longer served the Empire,<ref name="TFA" /> which had fallen in [[5 ABY]],<ref name="Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> and instead served as a member of the [[Resistance]], a successor of the Rebel Alliance who [[First Order-Resistance War|opposed]] the [[First Order]], a successor state of the Empire. R2-Q2 was stationed at the [[Resistance base]] on the planet [[D'Qar]] and, after the Resistance victory at the [[Battle of Starkiller Base]], R2-Q2 was part of the crowd that gathered to watch the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]'', a [[YT-1300 light freighter]], leave to seek out the [[Jedi]] Master [[Luke Skywalker]].<ref name="TFA" /> Shortly after the ''Falcon'' departed, the base on D'Qar was evacuated and then destroyed.<ref name="TLJ">{{Film|VIII}}</ref>

==Characteristics==
R2-Q2 had [[Color|black]], gray, and white plating and a black [[sensor]].<ref name="A New Hope" /> It stood 0.96 [[meter]]s (3[[Foot|ft]], 2in) tall.<ref name="Height" />

==Behind the scenes==
R2-Q2 first appeared in the [[1977]] [[original trilogy]] film, [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']].<ref name="A New Hope" /> The [[Star Wars: Build Your Own R2-D2 79|seventy-ninth]] issue of ''[[Star Wars: Build Your Own R2-D2]]'' published by [[De Agostini]] in [[August]] of [[2018]]<ref name="Date">{{WebCite|url=https://www.model-space.com/gb/r2-d2-full-kit.html|text=Build R2-D2 &#124; 1:2 Scale on De Agostini Model Space|archivedate=20170829020311}} indicates that issues of ''[[Star Wars: Build Your Own R2-D2]]'' was shipped in sets of four every month, and comments by consumers on the page state that approximately twenty-five issues had been sent out by [[June]] [[2021]]. As {{OfficialYouTube|channel=channel/UCa4lPqZo0FjN0--ieZve1uw|name=ModelSpace UK|video=XPJJsqgFMN8|text=Official ''Build Your Own R2-D2'' Build Diary &ndash; Issue 1}} states that the first issue was sent out in [[January]] of that year, issue 79 was released in [[August]] [[2018]].</ref> erroneously proclaimed that R2-Q2 was [[Biggs Darklighter]]'s [[R2-F2|astromech]] at the [[Battle of Yavin]].<ref name="BYO R2">{{BuildR2Cite|79|Droid Directory}}</ref>

